\f0\fs28\b \cf0 ============================================================\
HOW TO USE THIS FILE  -  Family Recipes Importer\
============================================================\b0\fs24\
\
This file is a staging area for new recipes.\
\
When ready to import, open Terminal and run:\
\
\f1    cd "/Users/garyburrell/Documents/Family Recipes/Family-Recipes-main"\
   python3 add_recipes.py\f0\
\
The script will:\
  - Parse every recipe below the ADD RECIPES line at the bottom\
  - Create an individual HTML page for each new recipe\
  - Update recipes.json and recipes-data.js automatically\
  - Skip any recipe already in the collection (safe to re-run)\
\
After a successful import, delete the recipes you just added\
(below the ADD RECIPES line) and save this file ready for next time.\
Keep this instructions block - it is automatically ignored by the script.\
\
\
\b ============================================================\
RECIPE FORMAT\
============================================================\b0\
\
Copy this template for each recipe. Fields are NOT case-sensitive.\
Separate multiple recipes with a line of three dashes: ---\
\
\f1 Recipe Title Here\
Category: <see list below>\
Source: <who the recipe is from>\
\
Ingredients:\
<one ingredient per line>\
\
Instructions:\
<free text - as many lines as you need>\
---\f0\
\
\b Available categories:\b0\
  Appetizers, Beverages, Breads, Cakes, Cookies, Desserts,\
  Main Dishes, Muffins, Pies & Tarts, Salads, Squares & Bars,\
  Soups, Sides, Condiments, Breakfast, Snacks\
  (or type any new category - it will be created automatically)\
\
\b Source examples:\b0\
  Mum, Grandma, Aunt Edna, Handwritten Note, Printed Cookbook,\
  Magazine Clipping, or any person/source name you like.\
\
\
\b ============================================================\
GEMINI AI PROMPTS\
============================================================\b0\
\
Use these prompts at gemini.google.com to convert recipes into the\
correct format. Copy the prompt, add your content, and paste the\
result into this file below the ADD RECIPES line.\
\
\
