\b ============================================================\
HOW THE PYTHON SCRIPT WORKS  (add_recipes.py)\
============================================================\b0\
\
The script lives in the same folder as this file:\
\f1   /Users/garyburrell/Documents/Family Recipes/Family-Recipes-main/add_recipes.py\f0\
\
\b Run it from Terminal:\b0\
\f1   cd "/Users/garyburrell/Documents/Family Recipes/Family-Recipes-main"\
   python3 add_recipes.py\f0\
\
  Or point it at a different RTF file:\
\f1   python3 add_recipes.py ~/Desktop/more_recipes.rtf\f0\
\
\
\b What the script does, step by step:\b0\
\
  1. READS this RTF file and strips all RTF formatting codes\
     to get plain text.\
\
  2. SKIPS everything above "ADD YOUR NEW RECIPES BELOW THIS LINE"\
     so instructions, prompts and examples are never imported.\
\
  3. SPLITS the remaining text into recipe blocks wherever it\
     finds a --- separator line.\
\
  4. PARSES each block looking for:\
       - First line (or "Title:" line)  ->  recipe title\
       - "Category:" line               ->  category tag\
       - "Source:" line                 ->  attribution\
       - "Ingredients:" section         ->  one ingredient per line\
       - "Instructions:" section        ->  free-form method text\
\
  5. CHECKS for duplicates against recipes.json. Any recipe\
     whose title already exists is skipped safely.\
\
  6. WRITES a new HTML file for each new recipe using the same\
     visual template as all the other recipe pages.\
     File name is derived from the recipe title, e.g.:\
       "Chocolate Chip Cookies"  ->  Chocolate Chip Cookies.html\
\
  7. UPDATES recipes.json - appends the new entries and re-sorts\
     the whole list alphabetically by title.\
\
  8. REGENERATES recipes-data.js from the updated recipes.json\
     so the site works when opened directly from the file system\
     (not just via a web server).\
\
  9. PRINTS a summary showing how many recipes were added,\
     skipped, or had errors.\
\
\
\b Files the script reads/writes:\b0\
\
  new_recipes.rtf    <-- this file (input, never modified)\
  recipes.json       <-- master recipe data (updated)\
  recipes-data.js    <-- JS version of same data (regenerated)\
  [Title].html       <-- one new HTML file per recipe (created)\
\
\
\b If something goes wrong:\b0\
\
  - Re-running the script is always safe - it skips duplicates.\
  - recipes.json is the source of truth. If an HTML file looks\
    wrong, delete it and the entry from recipes.json, fix the\
    recipe in this RTF file, and re-run.\
  - The original backup is saved in: original_backup.zip\
\
